Three more veto-only / notification-only events guarded on per-tick paths.

1. EntityInsideBlockEvent - 24 call sites across the generated block classes, all byte-identical:

     if (!new EntityInsideBlockEvent(entity.getBukkitEntity(), CraftBlock.at(level, pos)).callEvent()) { return; }

   Each allocates a CraftBlock and an event, and entityInside runs per entity per tick for anything
   standing in one of those blocks - bubble columns, cobwebs, berry bushes, fire, pressure plates,
   cactus, campfires, crops, portals. In water-heavy or farm-heavy areas this is continuous. The
   event can only veto, so with no listener the early return never happens.

   Because the line is emitted into two dozen generated classes, apply.py handles this one as a
   directory-wide replace with a minimum-hit assertion rather than a list of filenames, so it does
   not rot when upstream adds or removes a block class.

2. EntityEffectTickEvent - fires on every effect application tick for every entity carrying an
   effect. Building it meant a getBukkitLivingEntity() lookup plus a
   CraftPotionEffectType.minecraftHolderToBukkit() conversion. Veto-only, so with no listener the
   condition reduces to the vanilla check either way. Note the site is already gated behind
   shouldApplyEffectTickThisTick(), so this is per application rather than literally every tick.

3. ServerTickStartEvent and ServerTickEndEvent - two allocations every tick, forever, on a server
   with no listener for either. Small individually, but it is the one path guaranteed to run 20
   times a second for the life of the process.

   Verified functionally rather than by inspection: a plugin that listens to ServerTickEndEvent
   (benchmarks/atlas-bench) still collects a full sample set against a patched jar, so the guard
   does not suppress the event when something is actually listening.

--- a/leaf-server/src/minecraft/java/net/minecraft/world/level/block/*.java   (24 files)
+++ b/leaf-server/src/minecraft/java/net/minecraft/world/level/block/*.java
-        if (!new EntityInsideBlockEvent(entity.getBukkitEntity(), CraftBlock.at(level, pos)).callEvent()) { return; }
+        if (EntityInsideBlockEvent.getHandlerList().getRegisteredListeners().length != 0
+            && !new EntityInsideBlockEvent(entity.getBukkitEntity(), CraftBlock.at(level, pos)).callEvent()) { return; }

--- a/leaf-server/src/minecraft/java/net/minecraft/world/effect/MobEffectInstance.java
+++ b/leaf-server/src/minecraft/java/net/minecraft/world/effect/MobEffectInstance.java
-            && new EntityEffectTickEvent(target.getBukkitLivingEntity(), CraftPotionEffectType.minecraftHolderToBukkit(this.effect), this.amplifier).callEvent()
+            && (EntityEffectTickEvent.getHandlerList().getRegisteredListeners().length == 0
+                || new EntityEffectTickEvent(target.getBukkitLivingEntity(), CraftPotionEffectType.minecraftHolderToBukkit(this.effect), this.amplifier).callEvent())

--- a/leaf-server/src/minecraft/java/net/minecraft/server/MinecraftServer.java
+++ b/leaf-server/src/minecraft/java/net/minecraft/server/MinecraftServer.java
+        if (ServerTickStartEvent.getHandlerList().getRegisteredListeners().length != 0)
         new ServerTickStartEvent(this.tickCount+1).callEvent();
+        if (ServerTickEndEvent.getHandlerList().getRegisteredListeners().length != 0)
         new ServerTickEndEvent(this.tickCount, ..., remaining).callEvent();
